<p>Sections with a matching layer on <a href="{{ '/map/' | url }}">the map</a> have a "View on map" button. It opens the map in a new tab with the county highlighted and fitted, its boundary line on, the layers listed below switched on, and, for sea level rise, the matching increment (2, 4, 6, 8 or 10 feet; the button follows the slide's increment slider where it has one, and uses 2 feet where it has none). No map data is copied into County Profiles: the map loads every layer live from its publisher. Sections with no matching layer have no button: Homes at Risk (the map has no flood insurance claims layer), the sea level rise timing slide, and both economy topics. The flood-only counties get flood buttons only. On a dated snapshot page the button carries a note that the map shows current data, not that snapshot's.</p>
